# .reviewignore — paths to exclude from automated code review.
#
# Forward-compatible declaration. As of 2026-05-29 the in-use code-review
# skills (~/.claude/skills/code-review/ and the GSD /gsd-code-review
# workflow) do NOT yet consume this file — the GSD workflow uses a
# hardcoded exclude list (.planning/, *-SUMMARY.md, *-PLAN.md,
# *-VERIFICATION.md, ROADMAP.md, STATE.md, lock files), and the plugin
# /code-review is diff-scoped so excludes don't apply.
#
# Why publish this anyway:
#   1. Documents reviewer intent in-tree so it survives reviewer changes.
#   2. Each generated mirror file also carries an inline
#      "<!-- GENERATED — DO NOT EDIT. Source: shared/... -->" marker
#      (see scripts/sync-content.py); a savvy reviewer skips on either
#      signal.
#   3. Drops in cleanly when a future code-review skill learns
#      .reviewignore semantics (gitignore-style globs).
#
# Backlog item for the GSD skill repo (not this repo):
#   - Teach gsd-code-reviewer to parse .reviewignore before file
#     discovery. Estimated saving on a full-repo review here:
#     ~80K tokens (byte-identical first-principles/agents/ mirror of
#     shared/, verified 20/20 file pairs via diff -q).

# --- Generated agent-surface mirror (canonical source: shared/) ---
# Everything under first-principles/agents/ is generated by
# scripts/sync-content.py from shared/. Review the canonical source instead.
first-principles/agents/

# --- Generated focused-mode skill stubs (canonical source: shared/skills/) ---
# Bodies are generated by scripts/sync-content.py; frontmatter is the
# meaningful surface (description, disable-model-invocation, version) and
# is small enough to review directly via diff. Full body review duplicates
# shared/skills/<slug>/SKILL.md.
first-principles/skills/

# --- Planning artifacts (already excluded by GSD workflow + .gitignore) ---
# Listed here for completeness in case a future reviewer doesn't bake the
# exclusion in.
.planning/
